    "goal": "Measure first-pass hepatic extraction of diclofenac in a perfused liver-on-chip: dose at 0.5 mM (500 µM) inlet, quantify outlet at 0.35 mM (350 µM), and derive extraction ratio, clearance, and half-life.",
    "rationale": "Perfused liver-on-chip using primary human hepatocytes (PHH, BSL-2, gold-standard liver cell). Channel geometry 400 µm × 100 µm × 20 mm gives a flow rate of ~4 µL/min for a physiological hepatic sinusoidal shear of ~0.1 Pa (within the 0.05-0.15 Pa hepatic range). Diclofenac is dosed at 0.5 mM inlet (500 µM) with 0.35 mM outlet (350 µM), implying a first-pass extraction ratio E = 0.30 (intermediate extraction, Rowland & Tozer). Clearance Cl = E·Q and half-life t½ = ln2·V/Cl are computed from the flow rate and system volume. Medium viscosity taken as water-like (1e-3 Pa·s).",
